mangling)\n36: Set-Content -Path \"$env:TEMP\\nexlev_args.json\" -Value '{\"username\": \"EverythingProfessor\"}'\n37: ```\n38: \n39: ### Step 2: Run the caller script\n40: \n41: ```powershell\n42: python \"C:\\Users\\renu5\\.gemini\\config\\skills\\nexlev-mcp-caller\\scripts\\nexlev_call.py\" youtube_channel_about \"$env:TEMP\\nexlev_args.json\"\n43: ```\n44: \n45: ### Step 3: Parse the JSON output\n46: \n47: The script prints raw JSON text from NexLev. Parse it for your report.\n48: \n49: ---\n50: \n51: ## For Multiple Tool Calls (Batch Mode)\n52: \n53: Use the batch script to call multiple tools in one run:\n54: \n55: ```powershell\n56: # Create a batch config file\n57: Set-Content -Path \"$env:TEMP\\nexlev_batch.json\" -Value '[\n58:   {\"tool\": \"youtube_channel_about\", \"args\": {\"username\": \"SomeChannel\"}},\n59:   {\"tool\": \"youtube_channel_videos\", \"args\": {\"channel_id\": \"UC...\", \"sort_by\": \"popular\"}},\n60:   {\"tool\": \"check_channel_monetization\", \"args\": {\"channelId\": \"UC...\"}}\n61: ]'\n62: \n63: python \"C:\\Users\\renu5\\.gemini\\config\\skills\\nexlev-mcp-caller\\scripts\\nexlev_batch.py\" \"$env:TEMP\\nexlev_batch.json\"\n64: ```\n65: \n66: ---\n67: \n68: ## Available Scripts\n69: \n70: | Script | Purpose |\n71: |--------|---------|\n72: | `scripts/nexlev_call.py` | Call a single NexLev tool by name + args file |\n73: | `scripts/nexlev_batch.py` | Call multiple NexLev tools sequentially |\n74: | `scripts/nexlev_kill_stale.py` | Kill stale mcp-remote processes blocking port 28085 |\n75: \n76: ---\n77: \n78: ## NexLev Rate Limits (Free Plan) — CHECK BEFORE CALLING\n79: \n80: | Limit | Tools |\n81: |-------|-------|\n82: | **50/day** | youtube_search, youtube_channel_videos, youtube_channel_shorts, youtube_channel_playlists, youtube_channel_about |\n83: | **20/day** | latest_discovered_faceless_niches, search_youtube_suggested_videos, search_viral_videos_small_channels, faceless_outliers_videos |\n84: | **10/day** | channel_resolver, search_niche_finder_channels, search_videos, youtube_video_details, youtube_video_comments, youtube_channel_outliers, find_long_form_channels, find_shorts_channels, get_niche_finder_categories, get_niche_finder_formats |\n85: | **5/day** | get_similar_channels, check_faceless_channel, get_similar_videos, get_video_transcript, get_bulk_video_transcripts, get_video_subtitle, get_bulk_video_subtitles, get_similar_thumbnails, get_channel_analytics, get_daily_analytics, get_short_vs_long_views, get_geography_revenue, get_batch_channel_metrics, check_channel_monetization, check_video_monetization, get_video_rpm, get_niche_overview, get_niche_finder_tags, get_channel_promotions |\n86: | **2/day** | get_channel_promotions_realtime |\n87: | **1/day** | watch_youtube_video_and_ask, watch_instagram_video_and_ask, watch_tiktok_video_and_ask |\n88: | **0/day (Paid only)** | get_content_owner, search_cms_networks, swipefile tools, my_channel tools, generate/edit_thumbnail |\n89: \n90: ### Rate Limit Strategy\n91: 1. **ALWAYS start with 50/day tools** (youtube_channel_about → youtube_channel_videos)\n92: 2. **Use 5/day tools sparingly** — ask the user before burning get_channel_analytics\n93: 3. **If RATE LIMIT EXCEEDED** — tell the user which tool, suggest waiting 24h or enabling NexLev usage credits\n94: \n95: ### Full rate limit reference file\n96: `C:\\Users\\renu5\\Downloads\\Nexlev's official rate-limt mcp.md`\n97: \n98: ---\n99: \n100: ## Troubleshooting\n101: \n102: | Problem | Fix |\n103: |---------|-----|\n104: | `server name nexlev not found` from call_mcp_tool | Use this skill's Python scripts instead |\n105: | `RATE LIMIT EXCEEDED` | Check table above. Wait 24h or enable credits at nexlev.io |\n106: | Auth window doesn't open / \"Another instance running\" | Run `nexlev_kill_stale.py` then retry |\n107: | `Connection closed` | Stale mcp-remote process. Run `nexlev_kill_stale.py` then retry |\n108: | First time ever / tokens expired | Browser auth window will open automatically — complete it |\n109: | `npx` not found | Scripts already use `npx.cmd` — this is handled |\n110: \n111: ---\n112: \n113: ## OAuth Token Cache\n114: \n115: After first browser authorization, tokens are cached at:\n116: - `C:\\Users\\renu5\\.mcp-auth\\` (or similar npm cache location)\n117: - Tokens survive across conversations — you only auth once\n118: \n119: ---\n120: \n121: ## Channel Workflow Template\n122: \n123: Standard workflow for analyzing a channel:\n124: \n125: 1. `youtube_channel_about` (50/day) → Get channel ID, subs, views, join date, links\n126: 2. `youtube_channel_videos` with `sort_by: \"popular\"` (50/day) → Top videos\n127: 3. `check_channel_monetization` (5/day) → Monetized?\n128: 4. `check_faceless_channel` (5/day) → Faceless?\n129: 5. `get_channel_analytics` (5/day) → Growth, revenue estimates — **save this for last, only if needed**\n130: \nThe above content shows the entire, complete file contents of the requested file.\n"}
