,\"required\":[\"channelId\"],\"type\":\"object\"}}\nThe above content shows the entire, complete file contents of the requested file.\n"}
{"step_index":9,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-15T10:55:00Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-15T16:25:00+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-09-15T16:25:01+05:30\nFile Path: `file:///C:/Users/renu5/.gemini/antigravity/mcp/vidiq/vidiq_similar_channels.json`\nTotal Lines: 1\nTotal Bytes: 7514\nShowing lines 1 to 1\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: {\"name\":\"vidiq_similar_channels\",\"description\":\"Find COMPETITORS of a channel — either the user's own channel or a specific named channel. Uses neural semantic search tuned for competitor matching; the user's own authorized channels are automatically excluded from legacy manual-mode results.\\n\\nUse this tool ONLY when someone asks for competitors or similar channels relative to a channel:\\n- \\\"Who are my competitors?\\\" or \\\"Find channels like mine\\\" (the user's own channel — country/language are auto-detected in manual mode)\\n- \\\"Channels similar to [channel]\\\", \\\"Competitors of [channel]\\\", or \\\"Channels like @handle\\\" (a named reference channel)\\n\\nDo NOT use this tool for generic channel discovery by topic, size, growth, or any other criteria (\\\"find tech review channels\\\", \\\"top gaming channels in Brazil\\\", \\\"fastest growing fitness channels\\\") — use vidiq_channel_search for that.\\n\\nChoose exactly one mode: channelId or niche.\\n\\nADDITIVE CHANNEL ID MODE — when a canonical YouTube channel ID beginning with UC was supplied or already resolved, pass only channelId, plus optional size and sort. Do not copy resolved channel characteristics into this request or add niche/manual filters. Do not call vidiq_channel_search when a canonical ID is already available. A handle or URL must be resolved externally to a canonical channel ID before using this mode. The API derives the source classification and search tuning and excludes the reference channel.\\n\\nLEGACY MANUAL NICHE MODE — Legacy manual niche behavior is unchanged. The niche parameter is required in this mode — always provide a clear topic or content theme. All existing manual inputs remain supported, including minSubscribers, maxSubscribers, avgViews, avgViewsMin, avgViewsMax, country, language, channelType, faceless, and excludeChannelIds.\\n\\nSIMILAR TO A SPECIFIC CHANNEL IN LEGACY MANUAL MODE — when using the existing manual path, do NOT guess the reference channel's characteristics. Supply the same fields as before:\\n- niche: the reference channel's niche + subNiches, comma-separated (e.g. 'YouTube Growth, Monetization \\u0026 SEO')\\n- country: the reference channel's country\\n- language: the first code from the reference channel's languages\\n- channelType: the reference channel's channelType\\n- faceless: the reference channel's isFaceless value\\n- minSubscribers / maxSubscribers: a band around its subscriberCount, roughly 10% as min and 5x as max, unless the user asks for a specific range\\n- avgViews: the reference channel's avgViews; do not also set avgViewsMin/avgViewsMax unless the user asks for a specific range\\n- excludeChannelIds: the reference channel's channelId\\n\\nOmit sort for normal similarity ranking. When the user asks to rank these competitors by size or recent growth, set sort to subscriberCount, subsGrowth30d, or viewsGrowth30d; all explicit sorts reorder only the requested top similarity results.\\n\\nResults include the metrics used for sorting plus channel type and faceless status. In manual niche mode, country is a ranking preference rather than a strict filter, while language filters the language channels publish in. When omitted, country and language are auto-detected from the user's authorized channel.\\n\\nCost: 5 credit(s) per call.\",\"parameters\":{\"$schema\":\"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\",\"properties\":{\"avgViews\":{\"description\":\"The reference channel's lifetime average views per video (total views / total videos). When searching for competitors of a specific channel, pass its avgViews here so results are auto-ranged to a similar per-video-views league (parallels passing the reference channel's subscriber band). Leave unset for generic niche searches.\",\"minimum\":0,\"type\":\"number\"},\"avgViewsMax\":{\"description\":\"Manual upper bound for lifetime average views per video (total views / total videos), overriding the avgViews auto-range. Use together with avgViewsMin to define a specific per-video average-views range.\",\"minimum\":0,\"type\":\"number\"},\"avgViewsMin\":{\"description\":\"Manual lower bound for lifetime average views per video (total views / total videos), overriding the avgViews auto-range. Use to require results that average at least this many views per video — e.g. 50000 for '50k+ average views'. This is the per-video average, not total views.\",\"minimum\":0,\"type\":\"number\"},\"channelId\":{\"description\":\"Canonical YouTube channel ID beginning with UC. It is passed directly to the Similar Channels API without a resolution request.\",\"pattern\":\"^UC[A-Za-z0-9_-]{22}$\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"channelType\":{\"description\":\"Reference channel format. 'long' prefers long and mixed candidates; 'short' prefers short and mixed candidates; 'mixed' is neutral. This affects ranking, not eligibility.\",\"enum\":[\"long\",\"short\",\"mixed\"],\"type\":\"string\"},\"country\":{\"description\":\"Two-letter ISO 3166-1 country code used to prefer channels BASED IN that country — e.g. 'US', 'GB', 'BR', 'JP'. Matching channels receive a ranking boost, but channels based elsewhere may still appear. This is where the channel is located — NOT the audience/viewer country, and NOT the channel's language (use `language` to filter by language). When omitted, the country is auto-detected from the user's authorized channel (if any).\",\"maxLength\":2,\"minLength\":2,\"type\":\"string\"},\"excludeChannelIds\":{\"description\":\"Manual niche mode only: channel IDs to exclude from results. The user's own authorized channels are excluded automatically and do not need to be listed.\",\"items\":{\"minLength\":1,\"type\":\"string\"},\"maxItems\":50,\"type\":\"array\"},\"faceless\":{\"description\":\"Reference channel faceless status. When provided, candidates with the same status receive a ranking boost; other candidates remain eligible.\",\"type\":\"boolean\"},\"language\":{\"description\":\"Two-letter ISO 639-1 language code to filter results to channels whose content is in that language — e.g. 'en', 'es', 'pt', 'ja'. Pass the user's requested content language here (the language the channel publishes in — this is the channel's language, not its country). Only a single language is accepted. When omitted, the language is auto-detected from the user's authorized channel (if any).\",\"pattern\":\"^[A-Za-z]{2}$\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"maxSubscribers\":{\"description\":\"Upper bound for subscriber count. Use to filter out larger channels — e.g. 1000000 to cap results at channels under 1M subscribers. Use together with minSubscribers to define a specific range.\",\"maximum\":9007199254740991,\"minimum\":1,\"type\":\"integer\"},\"minSubscribers\":{\"description\":\"Lower bound for subscriber count. Use to filter out smaller channels — e.g. 10000 to only see channels with 10k+ subscribers. Use together with maxSubscribers to define a specific range.\",\"maximum\":9007199254740991,\"minimum\":0,\"type\":\"integer\"},\"niche\":{\"description\":\"Manual niche, topic, or content theme to search in. Use natural language — e.g. 'tech reviews' or 'vegan cooking tutorials'. Provide either this or channelId, not both; prefer channelId for a specific reference channel.\",\"minLength\":1,\"type\":\"string\"},\"size\":{\"default\":30,\"description\":\"Number of similar channels to return. Defaults to 30, maximum 50.\",\"maximum\":50,\"minimum\":1,\"type\":\"integer\"},\"sort\":{\"description\":\"Optional descending sort of the requested top similarity results: subscriberCount, subsGrowth30d, or viewsGrowth30d. Omit to keep neural similarity relevance order.\",\"enum\":[\"subscriberCount\",\"subsGrowth30d\",\"viewsGrowth30d\"],\"type\":\"string\"}},\"type\":\"object\"}}\nThe above content shows the entire, complete file contents of the requested file.\n"}
{"step_index":6,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-15T10:54:50Z","content":"Now let me read the NexLev MCP caller skill and check the tool schemas I'll need:","tool_calls":[{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"C:\\Users\\renu5\\.gemini\\config\\skills\\nexlev-mcp-caller\\SKILL.md","toolAction":"Reading skill file","toolSummary":"NexLev MCP caller skill"}},{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"C:\\Users\\renu5\\.gemini\\antigravity\\mcp\\vidiq\\vidiq_channel_stats.json","toolAction":"Reading tool schema","toolSummary":"VidIQ channel stats schema"}},{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"C:\\Users\\renu5\\.gemini\\antigravity\\mcp\\vidiq\\vidiq_similar_channels.json","toolAction":"Reading tool schema","toolSummary":"VidIQ similar channels schema"}},{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"C:\\Users\\renu5\\.gemini\\antigravity\\mcp\\vidiq\\vidiq_channel_videos.json","toolAction":"Reading tool schema","toolSummary":"VidIQ channel videos schema"}}]}
{"step_index":10,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-15T10:55:01Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-15T16:25:01+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-09-15T16:25:01+05:30\nFile Path: `file:///C:/Users/renu5/.gemini/antigravity/mcp/vidiq/vidiq_channel_videos.json`\nTotal Lines: 1\nTotal Bytes: 1397\nShowing lines 1 to 1\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: {\"name\":\"vidiq_channel_videos\",\"description\":\"Get videos from a YouTube channel by format (long-form, Shorts, or live streams). Use this when you already know which channel to look at. To discover videos across many channels, use vidiq_outliers or vidiq_trending_videos.\\n\\nUse vidiq_user_videos instead when the user needs their owned-channel library, private or unlisted videos, title search, privacy filters, or cursor pagination.\\n\\nUse this tool to:\\n- Browse a channel's recent uploads by video type (popular=false)\\n- Discover a channel's most popular videos by type (popular=true, default)\\n- Compare current views, likes, comments, views per hour (VPH), and breakout scores\\n- Get video metadata including titles, publish dates, thumbnails, and durations\\n\\nCost: 5 credit(s) per call.\",\"parameters\":{\"$schema\":\"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\",\"properties\":{\"channelId\":{\"description\":\"YouTube channel ID (e.g. 'UCX6OQ3DkcsbYNE6H8uQQuVA') or handle (e.g. '@MrBeast')\",\"minLength\":1,\"type\":\"string\"},\"popular\":{\"default\":true,\"description\":\"When true (default), returns the most popular videos. When false, returns recent uploads.\",\"type\":\"boolean\"},\"videoFormat\":{\"description\":\"Type of videos to retrieve: 'long' for long-form, 'short' for Shorts, 'live' for live streams\",\"enum\":[\"long\",\"short\",\"live\"],\"type\":\"string\"}},\"required\":[\"channelId\",\"videoFormat\"],\"type\":\"object\"}}\nThe above content shows the entire, complete file contents of the requested file.\n"}
{"step_index":12,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-15T10:55:11Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-15T16:25:11+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-09-15T16:25:12+05:30\nFile Path: `file:///C:/Users/renu5/.gemini/antigravity/mcp/vidiq/vidiq_outliers.json`\nTotal Lines: 1\nTotal Bytes: 5218\nShowing lines 1 to 1\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: {\"name\":\"vidiq_outliers\",\"description\":\"Find viral, breakout, and overperforming YouTube videos — videos getting significantly more views than their channel's average. Use this when someone asks for: viral videos, breakout hits, hidden gems, or videos blowing up. Use `keyword` to focus discovery on a topic, `channelIds` to focus on specific creators or competitors, or both to combine those constraints. For a general request that names neither a topic nor channels, the tool can return a broad outlier feed using the remaining filters and defaults. Filter requested content by the actual video-title `language`; `channelCountry` only filters where channels are based, not audience location or video language. For Polish-language outliers, pass `language='pl'`; `channelCountry='PL'` alone only restricts results to channels based in Poland. Returns a breakout score showing how much each video exceeds its channel's typical performance. For finding videos whose *thumbnails* look visually similar (by image or text description of the imagery), use vidiq_similar_thumbnails instead.\\n\\nCost: 5 credit(s) per call.\",\"parameters\":{\"$schema\":\"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\",\"properties\":{\"channelCountry\":{\"description\":\"Restrict to channels BASED IN this country, as an ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 code (e.g. \\\"PL\\\", \\\"US\\\"). This is where the channel/creator is located — NOT the audience/viewer country, and NOT the language of the videos. To search by the content language, use `language` instead. Example: for Polish-language outliers pass `language='pl'`; `channelCountry='PL'` alone only restricts to channels based in Poland (which may publish in any language).\",\"pattern\":\"^[A-Za-z]{2}$\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"channelIds\":{\"description\":\"Channel filter for focusing results on up to 50 specific creators or competitors. Each entry may be a channel ID (UC...), a handle (@MrBeast or MrBeast), or a channel URL — handles and URLs are resolved to channel IDs automatically. May be combined with `keyword`.\",\"items\":{\"minLength\":1,\"type\":\"string\"},\"maxItems\":50,\"minItems\":1,\"type\":\"array\"},\"contentType\":{\"default\":\"all\",\"description\":\"Filter by content type. Non-English title languages are available for long-form videos only: \\\"all\\\" is narrowed to \\\"long\\\", while \\\"short\\\" is rejected.\",\"enum\":[\"all\",\"long\",\"short\"],\"type\":\"string\"},\"keyword\":{\"description\":\"Topic filter for outlier video titles. Use it to focus results on a subject, and combine it with `channelIds` to search for that subject within selected channels.\",\"minLength\":1,\"type\":\"string\"},\"language\":{\"default\":\"en\",\"description\":\"Language of the video TITLE to search within, as a single ISO 639-1 code. Supported: en, es, ko, de, hi, ar, th, pl, it, ja, fr, tr, ru, pt, uk. When the user explicitly requests a language, always pass its code here. If the request does not specify a language, this tool defaults to language: \\\"en\\\" and searches English titles only. Non-English languages support long-form videos only: contentType: \\\"all\\\" is narrowed to \\\"long\\\", while contentType: \\\"short\\\" is rejected. For example: Spanish-language outliers → language: \\\"es\\\"; German breakout videos → language: \\\"de\\\"; \\\"видео на русском\\\" → language: \\\"ru\\\". Pass exactly one code (not a list); codes outside the supported set are rejected.\",\"enum\":[\"en\",\"es\",\"ko\",\"de\",\"hi\",\"ar\",\"th\",\"pl\",\"it\",\"ja\",\"fr\",\"tr\",\"ru\",\"pt\",\"uk\"],\"type\":\"string\"},\"limit\":{\"default\":20,\"description\":\"Number of results to return\",\"maximum\":100,\"minimum\":1,\"type\":\"integer\"},\"maxSubscribers\":{\"description\":\"Maximum channel subscribers\",\"maximum\":2147483647,\"minimum\":0,\"type\":\"integer\"},\"maxViews\":{\"description\":\"Maximum video views\",\"maximum\":2147483647,\"minimum\":0,\"type\":\"integer\"},\"minEngagementRate\":{\"description\":\"Minimum engagement rate\",\"type\":\"number\"},\"minOutlierScore\":{\"description\":\"Minimum outlier score\",\"type\":\"number\"},\"minSubscribers\":{\"description\":\"Minimum channel subscribers\",\"maximum\":2147483647,\"minimum\":0,\"type\":\"integer\"},\"minViews\":{\"description\":\"Minimum video views\",\"maximum\":2147483647,\"minimum\":0,\"type\":\"integer\"},\"minVph\":{\"description\":\"Minimum views per hour\",\"type\":\"number\"},\"publishedWithin\":{\"description\":\"Filter by publish date. For non-English languages, the effective window defaults to \\\"sixMonths\\\" and is capped there; English supports every listed range, including \\\"allTime\\\".\",\"enum\":[\"thisWeek\",\"thisMonth\",\"threeMonths\",\"sixMonths\",\"oneYear\",\"allTime\"],\"type\":\"string\"},\"requireAllTitleTerms\":{\"default\":false,\"description\":\"Set true to require every analyzed keyword term to match the video title. Recommended for person names, technical phrases, and narrow queries. Leave false for broader semantic discovery across titles, tags, and channel tags. Strict mode can return few or no results for non-English queries.\",\"type\":\"boolean\"},\"sort\":{\"description\":\"Sort field (defaults to score)\",\"enum\":[\"breakoutScore\",\"publishedAt\",\"viewCount\",\"vph\",\"score\"],\"type\":\"string\"},\"trendCategories\":{\"description\":\"Filter by trend category IDs (e.g. reaction, tier_list, mukbang). Use vidiq_trend_categories to list all available categories.\",\"items\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"type\":\"array\"}},\"type\":\"object\"}}\nThe above content shows the entire, complete file contents of the requested file.\n"}
{"step_index":13,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-15T10:55:12Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-15T16:25:12+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-09-15T16:25:13+05:30\nFile Path: `file:///C:/Users/renu5/.gemini/antigravity/mcp/vidiq/vidiq_channel_analytics.json`\nTotal Lines: 1\nTotal Bytes: 6032\nShowing lines 1 to 1\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: {\"name\":\"vidiq_channel_analytics\",\"description\":\"Get YouTube Analytics data for a channel you own — views, watch time, subscribers gained, likes, comments, retention, traffic sources, demographics, and revenue (monetized channels).\\n\\nCommon reports are available as one-word presets via `report`: audience_retention (per-video drop-off curve), traffic_sources, audience_demographics, audience_geography, revenue_report, top_videos, shorts_vs_longform_split. Or build custom queries with flexible date ranges, metric selection, and dimensional breakdowns (by day, country, device type, traffic source, etc.).\\n\\nUse this tool to:\\n- Analyze channel performance over a specific time period\\n- See where viewers drop off in a video (report='audience_retention' + filters='video==VIDEO_ID')\\n- Break down views by traffic source, country, device type, age/gender\\n- See which videos actually earn (report='revenue_report', dimensions=['video'])\\n- Compare Shorts vs long-form performance (report='shorts_vs_longform_split')\\n\\nNote: Only available for channels authorized to your account. Revenue metrics additionally require the channel to be monetized.\\n\\nCost: 5 credit(s) per call.\",\"parameters\":{\"$schema\":\"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\",\"properties\":{\"channelId\":{\"description\":\"YouTube channel ID (e.g. 'UCX6OQ3DkcsbYNE6H8uQQuVA') or handle (e.g. '@MrBeast')\",\"minLength\":1,\"type\":\"string\"},\"dimensions\":{\"description\":\"Dimensions to break down by (e.g. day, country, deviceType). month: startDate/endDate are snapped to the first of their month (YouTube requires month-aligned bounds). video, insightTrafficSourceDetail, insightPlaybackLocationDetail are top-N reports (ranked by views; pass sort/maxResults to change); the two *Detail dims also need a parent-type filter (insightTrafficSourceType== / insightPlaybackLocationType==). elapsedVideoTimeRatio (audience retention) needs a video== filter. Most dimensions can't be combined (YouTube supports only specific report shapes) — if a combo is rejected, request each dimension separately.\",\"items\":{\"enum\":[\"deviceType\",\"country\",\"video\",\"channel\",\"insightPlaybackLocationType\",\"insightPlaybackLocationDetail\",\"insightTrafficSourceDetail\",\"insightTrafficSourceType\",\"month\",\"day\",\"creatorContentType\",\"subscribedStatus\",\"gender\",\"ageGroup\",\"elapsedVideoTimeRatio\"],\"type\":\"string\"},\"type\":\"array\"},\"endDate\":{\"description\":\"End date (YYYY-MM-DD). Defaults to today\",\"format\":\"date\",\"pattern\":\"^(?:(?:\\\\d\\\\d[2468][048]|\\\\d\\\\d[13579][26]|\\\\d\\\\d0[48]|[02468][048]00|[13579][26]00)-02-29|\\\\d{4}-(?:(?:0[13578]|1[02])-(?:0[1-9]|[12]\\\\d|3[01])|(?:0[469]|11)-(?:0[1-9]|[12]\\\\d|30)|(?:02)-(?:0[1-9]|1\\\\d|2[0-8])))$\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"filters\":{\"description\":\"Filter expression (e.g. 'video==dQw4w9WgXcQ', 'country==US')\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"maxResults\":{\"description\":\"Maximum number of rows to return. insightTrafficSourceDetail and insightPlaybackLocationDetail allow at most 25 (default 25); video allows at most 200 (default 25); elapsedVideoTimeRatio requires at least 100 (default 100) because audience retention is a 100-point curve and does not have the video's 200-row ceiling.\",\"exclusiveMinimum\":0,\"maximum\":9007199254740991,\"type\":\"integer\"},\"metrics\":{\"description\":\"Metrics to retrieve. Default: views, estimatedMinutesWatched, subscribersGained, likes, comments. Some dimensions support only a restricted metric set — an unsupported metric is rejected, and omitted metrics narrow to the supported subset of the default. Each restricted dimension and the metrics it allows: insightTrafficSourceType, insightTrafficSourceDetail, insightPlaybackLocationType, insightPlaybackLocationDetail, deviceType → views, estimatedMinutesWatched, averageViewDuration, averageViewPercentage; subscribedStatus → those plus likes, dislikes, annotationClickThroughRate; ageGroup, gender → viewerPercentage; elapsedVideoTimeRatio → audienceWatchRatio, relativeRetentionPerformance, totalSegmentImpressions. For subscriber/comment metrics use a time/geo dimension (day, country).\",\"items\":{\"enum\":[\"views\",\"estimatedMinutesWatched\",\"averageViewPercentage\",\"averageViewDuration\",\"viewerPercentage\",\"estimatedRevenue\",\"subscribersGained\",\"subscribersLost\",\"likes\",\"dislikes\",\"comments\",\"audienceWatchRatio\",\"relativeRetentionPerformance\",\"totalSegmentImpressions\",\"estimatedAdRevenue\",\"estimatedRedPartnerRevenue\",\"grossRevenue\",\"cpm\",\"adImpressions\",\"monetizedPlaybacks\",\"playbackBasedCpm\",\"annotationClickThroughRate\"],\"type\":\"string\"},\"minItems\":1,\"type\":\"array\"},\"report\":{\"description\":\"Named report preset that fills metrics/dimensions/sort with a known-good YouTube Analytics report shape (explicitly-passed metrics/dimensions/sort/maxResults still win). audience_retention: per-video retention curve — REQUIRES filters='video==VIDEO_ID'. traffic_sources: views by source (search, suggested, browse, external...). audience_demographics: age/gender split (viewerPercentage). audience_geography: views by country. revenue_report: daily earnings (monetized channels only; combine with dimensions=['video'] for per-video earnings — YouTube does not support revenue by traffic source). top_videos: own videos ranked by views (pass sort='-estimatedRevenue' plus revenue metrics to rank by earnings instead). shorts_vs_longform_split: views/watch-time split between Shorts, long-form and live (creatorContentType).\",\"enum\":[\"audience_retention\",\"traffic_sources\",\"audience_demographics\",\"audience_geography\",\"revenue_report\",\"top_videos\",\"shorts_vs_longform_split\"],\"type\":\"string\"},\"sort\":{\"description\":\"Sort field, prefix with '-' for descending (e.g. '-views')\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"startDate\":{\"description\":\"Start date (YYYY-MM-DD). Defaults to 28 days ago\",\"format\":\"date\",\"pattern\":\"^(?:(?:\\\\d\\\\d[2468][048]|\\\\d\\\\d[13579][26]|\\\\d\\\\d0[48]|[02468][048]00|[13579][26]00)-02-29|\\\\d{4}-(?:(?:0[13578]|1[02])-(?:0[1-9]|[12]\\\\d|3[01])|(?:0[469]|11)-(?:0[1-9]|[12]\\\\d|30)|(?:02)-(?:0[1-9]|1\\\\d|2[0-8])))$\",\"type\":\"string\"}},\"required\":[\"channelId\"],\"type\":\"object\"}}\nThe above content shows the entire, complete file contents of the requested file.\n"}
{"step_index":11,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-15T10:55:02Z","content":"Good. Now I have all the context I need. Let me also check the vidIQ outliers and earnings tools schemas, then I'll launch the research operation.","tool_calls":[{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"C:\\Users\\renu5\\.gemini\\antigravity\\mcp\\vidiq\\vidiq_outliers.json","toolAction":"Reading tool schema","toolSummary":"VidIQ outliers schema"}},{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"C:\\Users\\renu5\\.gemini\\antigravity\\mcp\\vidiq\\vidiq_channel_analytics.json","toolAction":"Reading tool schema","toolSummary":"VidIQ channel analytics schema"}},{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"C:\\Users\\renu5\\.gemini\\antigravity\\mcp\\vidiq\\vidiq_video_earnings_estimate.json","toolAction":"Reading tool schema","toolSummary":"VidIQ earnings estimate schema"}}]}
